From f3c2eff07c1de2df40f6a98c815d01699c0c05f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 11:29:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 085/206] docs(shorebird): the flag's own comment said it was
 still blocked

print_shorebird_info's DEFINE_FLAG carried a comment explaining that the
gen_snapshot half was blocked and pointing at the spike README for why. Both
halves are implemented now and their eight lines match theirs, so the comment
was asserting the opposite of the truth to anyone reading the flag's
definition.

Rewritten to say where each half lives -- LinkClassTables and LinkObjectPools
in gen_snapshot, PrintShorebirdStats in the engine -- and to name the check
that holds the output there. The fact that it used to be blocked is kept in one
line, because a reader coming from the older notes will want to know the
verdict moved rather than wonder which is current.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc b/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
index d7da72eb668..7b8f63440df 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
@@ -58,10 +58,15 @@ DEFINE_FLAG(charp,
 // Their description string, verbatim. A bool, not a charp: their engine reads
 // it with `ldrb` and compares against 1.
 //
-// Both sides of the fork have one. In gen_snapshot it gates the three-stage
-// object-pool mapping report, which is still blocked -- see the spike README.
-// In the engine it gates Deserializer::PrintShorebirdStats, which is not, so
-// this is half implemented on purpose rather than by omission.
+// Both sides of the fork have one, and both are now implemented. In
+// gen_snapshot it gates the three-stage mapping report, printed once for the
+// class table and once for the object pool by ShorebirdLinker::LinkClassTables
+// and LinkObjectPools; in the engine it gates
+// Deserializer::PrintShorebirdStats.
+//
+// The gen_snapshot half was blocked for a long time and this comment used to
+// say so. Its eight lines now match theirs exactly on their own link-info
+// files -- see shorebird_info_check.sh in the spike.
 DEFINE_FLAG(bool,
             print_shorebird_info,
             false,
-- 
